* mixer-pumped-rf-admittance (issue #111) -- ONE nominal point:
* hbt_typ / 27 C / VDD = 2.50 V. Template: run_probe.py substitutes the model
* library path, the placeholder path, the two control fragments and the
* generated run blocks (the brace tokens below), then runs the result ONCE with
* `ngspice -b`. Single local process; no grid, no sweep, no loop outside the
* ngspice control language's own sequential runs.
*
* What this measures: the LO-on (pumped) small-signal RF-port admittance of the
* exploratory placeholder mixer, restricted to the wanted (f_u = 19.45 GHz) and
* image (f_l = 17.45 GHz) sidebands, as a 2x2 conjugate-coupled matrix, plus two
* known-answer fixtures that see the same perturbation parameters in the same
* runs. Deterministic input admittance only: nothing here is a noise figure,
* and nothing here is a row-5 compliance measurement.
*
* DUT: the placeholder mixer fragment included VERBATIM (one npn13G2, Nx=4;
* RF + LO summed at the base). Its own RF tones are zeroed (alterparam vrf=0),
* so its RF source resistor Rrf (z0 = 50 ohm, rfsrc -> prf) is a 50 ohm
* termination of the RF port. LO drive vlo = 0.08 V EMF is the placeholder's
* own value: a PROBE SETTING, not a qualified drive (issue #68).
*
* Port reference plane: node prf (the placeholder's RF port), looking into its
* 1 pF coupling capacitor Cin_rf towards the base. The perturbation is a Norton
* current per sideband (J = E/z0, E = {apu}, {apl}) injected into prf through a
* 0 V ammeter, in parallel with Rrf: identical to driving the port from a
* Thevenin EMF E through the placeholder's own 50 ohm, so the termination the
* mixer sees at every frequency is unchanged. Port current, positive INTO the
* mixer:  I = i(vpsense) + (v(rfsrc) - v(prf)) / 50.
*
* Projections: .meas INTEG (trapezoid) of v*cos / v*sin at f_u and f_l over the
* retained window [80, 120] ns and the extended window [80, 160] ns. Every tone
* is an integer multiple of 25 MHz, so each window holds an integer number of
* periods of f_u, f_l and f_LO and the projections are orthogonal.
.param apu=0 apl=0 phu=20 phl=70

* ---- DUT: the placeholder, included verbatim, and its Norton perturbation ----
.lib "/home/ubuntu/share/pdk/ihp-sg13g2/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerHBT.lib" hbt_typ
.temp 27
.param vdd_val=2.5
.include "/home/ubuntu/GitHub/sg13g2-sat-rx/.loom/worktrees/issue-111/sim/mixer-conversion-iip3/testbench/mixer_ce_placeholder.spice"
Ipu 0 pj DC 0 SIN(0 {apu/z0} 19.45e9 0 0 {phu})
Ipl 0 pj DC 0 SIN(0 {apl/z0} 17.45e9 0 0 {phl})
Vpsense pj prf DC 0


* ---- known-answer control fixtures (disjoint circuits) ----
* ---- inlined from sim/mixer-pumped-rf-admittance/controls/rc_known_answer.spice ----
* Known-answer control 1: a PASSIVE series RC port (linear, time-invariant).
* Driven exactly like the DUT port: a Norton perturbation current J = E/z0 per
* tone (E = {apu}, {apl}) injected through a 0 V ammeter into the port node, in
* parallel with the fixture's own z0 = 50 ohm source resistor to a 0 V node.
*   I_port = i(vksense) + (v(krs) - v(kp)) / 50     (positive into the RC)
* Closed form (pumped.rc_expected):
*   Y_uu = 1/(R + 1/(j w_u C)),  Y_ll = 1/(R + 1/(j w_l C)),  Y_ul = Y_lu = 0
* with R = 25 ohm, C = 1 pF. An LTI port has no conjugate (image) coupling, so the
* cross terms are a numerical null and the fixture must classify SCALAR_ADEQUATE.
Iku 0 kj DC 0 SIN(0 {apu/50} 19.45e9 0 0 {phu})
Ikl 0 kj DC 0 SIN(0 {apl/50} 17.45e9 0 0 {phl})
Vksense kj kp DC 0
Rks kp krs 50
Vkrs krs 0 DC 0
Ck kp kx 1p
Rk kx 0 25
* ---- end inlined control ----

* ---- inlined from sim/mixer-pumped-rf-admittance/controls/modulated_known_answer.spice ----
* Known-answer control 2: an IDEAL periodically modulated port (linear,
* periodically time-varying, memoryless conductance plus a shunt capacitor).
*   i(t) = (g0 + 2 g2 cos(2 w_LO t + th)) v(t) + Cm dv/dt + ib sin(w_u t + phb)
* Driven by an IDEAL voltage source (both sideband tones in series) through a
* 0 V ammeter, so the port voltage is exactly the applied tones and the closed
* form is exact (no other mixing frequency reaches the port voltage):
*   Y_uu = g0 + j w_u Cm,  Y_ll = g0 + j w_l Cm,  Y_ul = Y_lu = g2 e^{j th}
* (pumped.md_expected; g0 = 20 mS, Cm = 0.1 pF, g2 = 6 mS, th = 40 deg). The
* modulation at 2 f_LO maps f_u onto the conjugated image f_l and back, so
* |Y_ul|/|Y_uu| ~ 0.26: the fixture must classify MATRIX_REQUIRED, and a scalar
* extraction (sabotage omit_image) must fail it. The ib term is an LO-only
* (perturbation-independent) current at f_u that baseline subtraction must
* remove (sabotage no_baseline must fail). I_port = i(vmsense), positive into
* the modulated element.
.param mg0=0.02 mg2=0.006 mth=40 mib=1e-6 mphb=10
Vmu mu 0 DC 0 SIN(0 {apu} 19.45e9 0 0 {phu})
Vml mv mu DC 0 SIN(0 {apl} 17.45e9 0 0 {phl})
Vmsense mv mp DC 0
Bmd mp 0 I = ({mg0} + 2*{mg2}*cos(2*2*pi*18.45e9*time + {mth}*pi/180))*V(mp) + {mib}*sin(2*pi*19.45e9*time + {mphb}*pi/180)
Cmd mp 0 0.1p
* ---- end inlined control ----


.options savecurrents=0
.control
set noaskquit
set filetype=ascii
echo "MARK ngspice_banner_follows"
version -s
let wu = 2*pi*19.45e9
let wl = 2*pi*17.45e9

* ---- run base: amplitude=0 phu=20 phl=70 tmax=1e-12 ----
alterparam apu=0
alterparam apl=0
alterparam phu=20
alterparam phl=70
alterparam vrf=0
reset
tran 1e-12 1.6e-07 0 1e-12
let npts = length(time)
echo "MARK R_base_points=$&npts"
let pc = v(kp)*cos(wu*time)
let ps = v(kp)*sin(wu*time)
meas tran rc_v_base_w_u_c INTEG pc from=8e-08 to=1.2e-07
meas tran rc_v_base_w_u_s INTEG ps from=8e-08 to=1.2e-07
echo "MARK rc_v_base_w_u_c=$&rc_v_base_w_u_c rc_v_base_w_u_s=$&rc_v_base_w_u_s"
meas tran rc_v_base_x_u_c INTEG pc from=8e-08 to=1.6e-07
meas tran rc_v_base_x_u_s INTEG ps from=8e-08 to=1.6e-07
echo "MARK rc_v_base_x_u_c=$&rc_v_base_x_u_c rc_v_base_x_u_s=$&rc_v_base_x_u_s"
let pc = v(kp)*cos(wl*time)
let ps = v(kp)*sin(wl*time)
meas tran rc_v_base_w_l_c INTEG pc from=8e-08 to=1.2e-07
meas tran rc_v_base_w_l_s INTEG ps from=8e-08 to=1.2e-07
echo "MARK rc_v_base_w_l_c=$&rc_v_base_w_l_c rc_v_base_w_l_s=$&rc_v_base_w_l_s"
meas tran rc_v_base_x_l_c INTEG pc from=8e-08 to=1.6e-07
meas tran rc_v_base_x_l_s INTEG ps from=8e-08 to=1.6e-07
echo "MARK rc_v_base_x_l_c=$&rc_v_base_x_l_c rc_v_base_x_l_s=$&rc_v_base_x_l_s"
let pc = i(vksense)*cos(wu*time)
let ps = i(vksense)*sin(wu*time)
meas tran rc_i_base_w_u_c INTEG pc from=8e-08 to=1.2e-07
meas tran rc_i_base_w_u_s INTEG ps from=8e-08 to=1.2e-07
echo "MARK rc_i_base_w_u_c=$&rc_i_base_w_u_c rc_i_base_w_u_s=$&rc_i_base_w_u_s"
meas tran rc_i_base_x_u_c INTEG pc from=8e-08 to=1.6e-07
meas tran rc_i_base_x_u_s INTEG ps from=8e-08 to=1.6e-07
echo "MARK rc_i_base_x_u_c=$&rc_i_base_x_u_c rc_i_base_x_u_s=$&rc_i_base_x_u_s"
